=========================
Classic Warclient Ruleset
=========================

This is Warciv's competitive variant of Freeciv's classic ruleset. It keeps
the familiar classic game while restoring and extending Warclient-style play.

Highlights
----------

- Four base trade routes per city with a 2.00x Warclient-style recurring bonus
- Civ I/II-style research costs
- Square city radius and matching city vision
- Rapture-oriented city management presets
- Classic settler population costs and competitive terrain timings
- Support for Warciv's automatic caravan planning

The accompanying ``classic-warclient-competitive.serv`` profile supplies the
recommended map and server settings, including archipelago-shaped islands,
independent lake and river density, increased natural resources, and the
optional explainable ``ailargepox`` strategy for default AI players. Largepox
builds seven to eleven core cities according to available island land, plus one
support city. It places the core as a trade graph, establishes at least 80%
of its route capacity, and then attempts uninterrupted rapture growth in core
cities of size three or greater while continuing to fill remaining routes.
The research milestones are Trade, Republic, Construction, Democracy, and
Sanitation; population-limit buildings override additional caravans, and
route income can be reinvested immediately in missing routes and growth
buildings. Smaller islands reduce the city target; normal largepox islands
use remaining legal coastal gaps before switching fully to vertical growth.
If exploration temporarily exposes no useful site, the AI may start its trade
network and resume expansion in bounded windows when a valid site appears;
Settlers doing terrain work do not falsely count as pending cities. The largepox
settler evaluates the full future city radius, softly penalizes overlap, and
rewards sites which complete useful four-route partnerships instead of
accepting the first smallpox-style location nearby. The trade-network phase
is capped at 28 turns so difficult geography cannot stall growth forever.
During rapture the city manager reserves food, includes size-two cities in
the happiness plan for their next growth turn, and keeps a small luxury margin
so shared tiles do not repeatedly cancel celebration. It is enabled by
default when this ruleset is selected and can be disabled with
``/set ailargepox disabled``.

From a build directory, launch the server with:

  ./run.sh freeciv-server --read ../data/classic-warclient-competitive.serv

Or select the ruleset alone with:

  /ruleset classic-warclient
